WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.403
[music playing]

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:08.808 line:8%
Tonight on an epic
"Forged in Fire,"

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:13.146 line:8%
Marvel's Midnight
Suns take over.

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:14.647
Jessie, Paul, gentlemen,
congratulations.

00:00:14.713 --> 00:00:17.183
You are now vaulting into the
final round of this Marvel's

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.684
Midnight Suns competition.

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:20.352
In this final round, we're
sending you back to your home

00:00:20.452 --> 00:00:23.189
forges to bring yet
another iconic weapon

00:00:23.255 --> 00:00:25.190
from the Midnight Suns to life.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.626
To tell you more
about that, I want

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.560
to introduce you to the
game's creative director,

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.595
Jake Solomon.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.997 line:14%
I am.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:33.500 line:8%
Bladesmiths, we are so
excited for this next build,

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:36.435
a weapon that has never
existed in the Marvel universe

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:37.570
before now.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:43.108
Bladesmiths, you need to
go home and build this--

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:45.311
the Hunter's iconic blades.

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:48.113
[music playing]

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.383
Bladesmiths, this
pair of lethal swords

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.319
belongs to the Hunter,
an original superhero

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:56.055
that we created in close
partnership with Marvel.

00:00:56.121 --> 00:00:58.123
The Hunter is the
first customizable

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:01.127
hero in the Marvel universe.

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:04.063
Bladesmiths, we are really
excited to see you bring

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:05.831
these virtual blades to life.

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:06.933
Good luck.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.334
We will see you
here in four days.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:11.204 line:14%
[music playing]

00:01:13.138 --> 00:01:14.474
My name is Paul
[inaudible],, Junior.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.576 line:14%
I'm from Livonia, Texas.

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:18.645 line:14%
I'm 49 years old.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:21.180
I served 22 years in the Army.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.983
I run a program for vets
and first responders,

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:27.186
helping teach them
how to make knives.

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:31.123
If I were to be a superhero,
I would be Captain Damascus.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:33.259
I'd take all their blades
and make them cooler.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:37.129
I want to put my touch mark
on it as Captain Damascus.

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:38.931
So we're going to
make Damascus billets

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:42.768
with 80CrV2 and 15 and 20.

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:46.873
To tackle these brass guards,
I plan on using the mill.

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:48.707
All right, if I get
this milled, get

00:01:48.807 --> 00:01:51.978
this handle material to sit in.

00:01:52.044 --> 00:01:53.980
They're a little
difficult because they

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:57.883
are a matching set, one of them
being smaller than the other.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.652
I still have to
quench my blades.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:00.753
All right.

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:03.523
I'm ready to start
heat-treating.

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:06.291
Going in attack quench
is always scary.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:09.395
You could always come
out with a crack, a warp.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.930
This could be a major problem
for me this late in the game.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.501
[intense music]

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:17.136
Oh, yeah.

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:18.070
Good and straight.

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:20.240
[music playing]

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:23.809
All right.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.844
Two hard blades.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.078
Looking good.

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:27.613
So as the clock
comes to an end, I

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.184
need to hurry and get the
paint rays put on the blades.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.920
That's the best I can
do with what I got.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.122
That's it for now
from Captain Damascus.

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:37.123
We'll see you back at the forge.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:40.160 line:14%
[music playing]

00:02:42.294 --> 00:02:43.262
My name is Jessie Wipperman.

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:44.397
I'm 37 years old.

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:45.798 line:14%
And I'm from Des Moines, Iowa.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.868 line:8%
And I've been bladesmithing
for about five years.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.469
All of my kids
have tried forging,

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.672
but they realized how hot
it is, how dirty it is.

00:02:53.772 --> 00:02:56.709
And they decided that playing
video games is more fun.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:03:00.980
If I had a Marvel superhero
name, it would be the Foundry.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.415
The Foundry's powers
melt the competition.

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:05.284
[laughs]

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:09.088
I decided to go
with mono steel 8670

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:11.490
because I feel like
spending more time,

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:14.894
making sure that the
handle is the best handle

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.629
the judges have ever seen.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:20.433
I'm going to start
cutting the faux ivory

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:22.534
for my handles and the brass.

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:26.105
Now I'm just making sure that
everything pieces together

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.141
properly.

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:30.542
Biggest handle I've
ever done by far.

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:35.047
I'm going to be using the Dremel
to add some embellishments

00:03:35.113 --> 00:03:37.550
on the brass guard and pommel.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.853
I want the handles to
be the star of the show.

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:44.656
I'm excited to have the
judges test out my blades.

00:03:44.723 --> 00:03:47.226
And I'm sure that they'll
cut through anything

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:49.996
that they put in front of it.

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:53.366
Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:03:53.432 --> 00:03:57.970
Unfortunately, healing powers
is not my greatest suit,

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.539
but delegation of work is.

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:03.175
Wielding your weapons today
is my brother RJ Marquita.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:06.211
[music playing]

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:07.847
Jessie, you're up first.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:11.417
I am very proud of the blades
that I made going into testing.

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:13.085
I'm feeling pretty
confident right now.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:16.789
[intense music]

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:43.516
All right, Jessie, both
your long and short sword

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:45.318
are very comfortable to wield.

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:48.387
They've got a very nice balance.

00:04:48.453 --> 00:04:51.223
Now, your edges are very sharp.

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:54.192
They cut deeply into
the pig carcass.

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:57.997
Your weapons, sir,
they will kill.

00:04:58.064 --> 00:04:59.231
Thank you.

00:04:59.331 --> 00:05:00.266
Paul, your turn, sir.

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.467
Are you ready?

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:02.968
- I'll fire up the grill.
- All right.

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:03.936
We'll see you there.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:07.440
[intense music]

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:29.695
I saw that he held
back [inaudible]..

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:31.097
All right, Paul.

00:05:31.163 --> 00:05:33.799
First up for the long sword,
despite having the brass here,

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:35.902
and what I would think
is a counterbalance,

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.370
it is forward-heavy.

00:05:37.437 --> 00:05:41.440
Now, where my hand is, right
above here on the handle,

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:43.942
it digs into your palm.

00:05:44.042 --> 00:05:48.146
The shorter sword is much easier
to wield because the handle

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.414
matches nicely.

00:05:49.514 --> 00:05:52.585
But these are deep cuts
on the pig carcass.

00:05:52.651 --> 00:05:55.854
And overall, both of
your weapons will kill.

00:05:55.921 --> 00:05:56.856
Thank you.

00:05:56.923 --> 00:05:59.691
[music playing]

00:05:59.791 --> 00:06:01.627
Bladesmiths, welcome
to the strength test.

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:03.829
[intense music]

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:06.331
To test the strength and
durability of your blades,

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:08.634
I'm going to be bashing
them into that big thing,

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:10.269
and also check
for edge retention

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:12.371
by cutting through
these bags and our jugs.

00:06:12.437 --> 00:06:14.107
But I'm not going
to do this alone.

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:16.008
The Midnight Suns
work best as a team.

00:06:16.074 --> 00:06:19.445
So I'm going to enlist the help
of my teammate, Dave Baker.

00:06:19.511 --> 00:06:21.147
Jessie, you're up first.
Are you ready?

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:22.147
Give it hell.

00:06:22.214 --> 00:06:23.149
All right.

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:26.486
[intense music]

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:06.859
All right, Jessie, man.

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:08.160
This is a beautiful set.

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:12.698
For the smaller sword, it
took some dinging on the edge,

00:07:12.798 --> 00:07:14.433
but the weight is really nice.

00:07:14.533 --> 00:07:16.068
Dave really enjoyed
swinging this one.

00:07:16.168 --> 00:07:20.906
On the longer one, it took some
serious bending in the tests.

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:24.043
It's kicked off from the
handle, and then it kicks

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:25.978
back over at the tip there.

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:27.579
It was obviously sharp.

00:07:27.679 --> 00:07:30.549
I mean, both of these swords
cut like they're supposed to.

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:33.285
But there's no getting
around this significant bend

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:35.021
in the larger one here.

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:36.188
All right, Paul.
You're up next.

00:07:36.255 --> 00:07:37.989
Are you ready?
- Do it to it.

00:07:38.056 --> 00:07:38.958
All righty.

00:07:39.025 --> 00:07:42.595
[intense music]

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:17.429
All right, Paul.

00:08:17.529 --> 00:08:19.965 line:8%
So in Midnight Suns,
the video game,

00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:23.503 line:8%
Hunter carries these one in each
hand and uses them in battle.

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:25.470
And I don't know how long
I could swing this thing,

00:08:25.537 --> 00:08:26.472
to be honest with you.

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:28.373
It's just got so
much mass to it.

00:08:28.473 --> 00:08:29.908
And it's difficult to control.

00:08:30.008 --> 00:08:34.747
Also, your edge on the small
one took quite a bit of packing.

00:08:34.813 --> 00:08:38.617
It's quite dull here, which
changed the way that they cut.

00:08:38.717 --> 00:08:43.288
They're just not the cleanest
cuts, but they do smash.

00:08:43.355 --> 00:08:44.289
Nice shot.

00:08:44.356 --> 00:08:46.592
Thank you.

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:49.328
Bladesmiths, you started
off by making Blade's glaive

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:52.265
and ended with two
Hunter's iconic swords.

00:08:52.331 --> 00:08:54.066
But in this competition,
only one of you

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:56.301
can come out on top as a
Forged in Fire Champion

00:08:56.401 --> 00:08:57.803
of our Marvels
Midnight Suns takeover

00:08:57.903 --> 00:08:59.272
and getting a check for $10,000.

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:02.107
Today's Forged in
Fire Champion is--

00:09:02.174 --> 00:09:04.277
[intense music]

00:09:06.378 --> 00:09:07.313
Jessie.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.914
Congratulations.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.216
Paul, you impressed the judges,
but fortunately your blades

00:09:11.316 --> 00:09:12.284
did not make the cut.

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:13.885
And Ben is going
to tell you why.

00:09:13.952 --> 00:09:15.821
Paul, the fit and
finish on your handles

00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:18.090
is a little less refined
than your competitor.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:21.293
That, coupled with the fact that
your long sword is extremely

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.728
heavy and difficult to wield,
and your short sword took

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:25.530
some damage in
the strength test,

00:09:25.597 --> 00:09:26.932
are the reason we're
letting you go.

00:09:26.998 --> 00:09:28.400
Well, Paul, it's been
a pleasure watching

00:09:28.467 --> 00:09:29.735
you working this forge.

00:09:29.801 --> 00:09:31.003
But unfortunately, at
this point in time,

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:32.204
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:09:32.271 --> 00:09:33.538
step off the forge floor.

00:09:33.605 --> 00:09:35.107
Thank you for having me.

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:36.541
Good job.

00:09:36.608 --> 00:09:38.110
Jessie, congratulations.

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:40.645
That makes you the "Forged in
Fire" Champion of our Midnight

00:09:40.712 --> 00:09:42.415
Suns competition take over.

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:44.082
And you'll be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:09:44.149 --> 00:09:46.018
[applause]

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:47.552
This whole experience
has been a blast.

00:09:47.619 --> 00:09:49.521
And I would definitely
do it again.

00:09:49.621 --> 00:09:52.425
Marvel theme, giant
demon things, the judges

00:09:52.525 --> 00:09:55.261
are testing at the same
time, this is amazing.

00:09:55.361 --> 00:09:56.261
[applause]

00:09:56.362 --> 00:09:57.429
How do you feel?

00:09:57.529 --> 00:09:59.431
- Speechless.
- Yeah?

00:09:59.498 --> 00:10:00.599
I'm Jessie Wipperman.

00:10:00.665 --> 00:10:02.468
And I'm a "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:10:02.568 --> 00:10:03.502
And it feels amazing.

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:06.839
[music playing]

